// run
// #6265: a generic function called with a closure that captures a STATIC
// method reached through the CALLER's OWN generic type parameter —
// `T.__fromRow` inside `Box<T: Tabled>`, `T` bound via SPEC §11.3's
// Self-typed static dispatch — used to fail lowering, not checking:
//
//   error[E0092]: cannot lower a `.` field access on a receiver that is not
//   a class or interface
//
// pointing inside the closure, after `bit check` exited 0. Root cause: the
// interface's own `Self`-typed signature (`checktype.bit`'s `selfTypeId`,
// minted once per module) never gets bound to the CALLER's own type
// parameter when a static call is reached through a bound generic
// (`checkexprcall.bit`'s `staticReceiverType` resolves a type-param
// receiver through its CONSTRAINT INTERFACE, so `methodCallResult` answers
// with the interface's raw, unbound `Self!` signature) — so the closure
// LITERAL's own inferred function type kept `Self` unbound forever, and no
// generic instantiation's substitution env (keyed on `T`, never on `Self`)
// could ever fix it. A DIRECT `T.__fromRow(x)` call (no closure) escaped
// this entirely: lowering re-derives its result fresh from the SUBSTITUTED
// concrete receiver rather than reading the checker's cached type.
// `staticCallResultThroughReceiver` (checkexprcall.bit) now rebinds `Self`
// to the type parameter's own id before returning, so `nodeType`'s generic
// substitution (lower.bit) can turn it into the concrete instantiation's
// own type same as the direct call already did.
//
// A second, independent gap in the same shape: `lowerReachableSynthStatics`
// (#6260, compiler/lowermethodtable.bit) decides whether a `@table` class's
// synthesized static needs emitting by scanning `funcs` for a caller —
// but a closure literal lowered inside a Pass A3 method body lands in
// `lowerer.closureFuncs`, a separate list Pass A4 only merges into `funcs`
// AFTER that scan already ran, so a synthesized static reached ONLY through
// a closure stayed pruned and its call site linked to nothing. Fixed by
// scanning `lowerer.closureFuncs` too.
//
// `Box<T: Tabled>` here is `pkg/orm`'s `Repo<T: Tabled>` shape, minimized:
// `build` passes a closure over `T.__fromRow` into an UNRELATED generic
// function (`apply<A, R>`), mirroring `Repo<T>.find`/`all`/`first` handing
// one to `std/sql/row.bit`'s `sqlFindOne`/`sqlFindMany`.
interface Tabled {
  static __fromRow(x: int): Self!,
}

class Box<T: Tabled> {
  export build(x: int): T! {
    return apply(x, (n) => T.__fromRow(n))?
  }
}

fn apply<A, R>(x: A, f: (A) => R!): R! {
  return f(x)?
}

class Person {
  x: int

  static __fromRow(x: int): Person! {
    return Person{ x = x }
  }
}

fn main(): ()! {
  let b = Box<Person>{}
  let p = b.build(5)?
  print("${p.x}\n")
}
